WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:03.810
<i>I worked as a salaryman 
for a toxic company,</i>

00:03.810 --> 00:05.690
<i>until I reincarnated...</i>

00:05.690 --> 00:09.860
<i>in a crazy world where everything is 
dropped by monsters in dungeons.</i>

00:10.430 --> 00:15.080
<i>In my new life, I'm level 1, 
but I have a unique skill</i>

00:15.080 --> 00:17.210
<i>that puts all of my drop rates at rank S.</i>

00:17.730 --> 00:19.880
<i>And today I'm...</i>

00:19.880 --> 00:23.000
<i>dealing with </i>another<i> gorilla 
while trying to get my license?!</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:26.850
<i>And then I meet a mysterious 
girl who uses fire magic...</i>

00:26.850 --> 00:29.010
<i>What the heck is about to happen?!</i>

00:36.180 --> 00:45.270
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>A Beautiful Girl Appears</b>

02:06.570 --> 02:10.580
I got some new drops today: watermelons. 
Could you appraise them?

02:13.060 --> 02:15.430
Wow, that's a nice watermelon!

02:15.430 --> 02:17.190
You've done it again, Ryota!

02:17.420 --> 02:20.500
Give me just a minute while 
I head to the back and prepare...

02:20.500 --> 02:22.130
There'll be no need for that.

02:24.970 --> 02:27.770
I'll assess your goods right here and now.

02:27.770 --> 02:28.530
Eric!

02:29.180 --> 02:30.240
Let's see...

02:33.360 --> 02:38.090
Its refreshing texture and sweet flavor 
make my very soul feel fulfilled.

02:38.750 --> 02:44.340
It's like I'm on the beach in midsummer, 
with the sun blazing down on me!

02:44.340 --> 02:47.460
What? Watermelons from the guy 
who makes Ryota's Bamboo Shoots?

02:47.460 --> 02:49.820
First bamboo shoots, and now watermelons?!

02:49.820 --> 02:51.360
I want a bite, too!

02:51.360 --> 02:54.820
Hey! Stop it! That's mine!

02:56.010 --> 02:56.810
Ryota!

02:57.030 --> 03:01.240
Please let us sell these Ryota's Watermelons 
through an exclusive contract, too!

03:01.610 --> 03:02.820
Sure...

03:05.100 --> 03:08.380
<i>Wow... The watermelon's just as 
popular as the bamboo shoots!</i>

03:08.680 --> 03:12.580
All right! There's another  
reliable source of income!

03:12.580 --> 03:14.210
Oh, Ryota...

03:14.450 --> 03:17.750
Watermelons are dropped on the 
level 5 of Telulu, right?

03:17.750 --> 03:18.600
Yeah.

03:18.600 --> 03:20.560
Have you gotten your license already?

03:21.090 --> 03:22.160
License?

03:22.160 --> 03:27.100
Yes. It gives you permission to
 explore dungeons levels lower than level 6.

03:27.380 --> 03:29.520
It works for all dungeons across the world.

03:29.520 --> 03:31.790
Since dungeons get more 
dangerous every five levels,

03:31.790 --> 03:33.800
different towns have different policies.

03:33.800 --> 03:34.520
Uh-huh.

03:34.480 --> 03:39.110
<b>Safe</b>

03:34.480 --> 03:39.110
<b>Dangerous</b>

03:34.480 --> 03:39.110
<b>No License Needed</b>

03:34.480 --> 03:39.110
<b>License 1</b>

03:34.480 --> 03:39.110
<b>License 2</b>

03:34.520 --> 03:37.540
In Secro, there's a new 
license every five levels,

03:37.540 --> 03:41.010
and traders aren't permitted to 
buy items dropped in those levels

03:37.690 --> 03:42.950
<b>Dangerous</b>

03:37.690 --> 03:42.950
<b>No License Needed</b>

03:37.690 --> 03:42.950
<b>License 1</b>

03:37.690 --> 03:42.950
<b>License 2</b>

03:41.010 --> 03:42.960
if the adventurer doesn't have 
the appropriate license.

03:42.960 --> 03:44.420
I see.

03:44.420 --> 03:48.010
That would stop people from putting themselves 
in danger to get more valuable drops.

03:48.010 --> 03:49.790
Right. So...

03:49.790 --> 03:53.210
I recommend getting a license to 
make things easier in the future.

03:55.020 --> 03:56.540
So this is the place?

03:57.640 --> 03:58.960
Excuse me.

04:03.450 --> 04:06.470
Is this where I can get a license?

04:09.210 --> 04:10.470
Your achievements?

04:10.470 --> 04:11.300
Huh?

04:12.140 --> 04:14.010
When they ask about your achievements...

04:14.450 --> 04:15.300
Oh, uh...

04:15.680 --> 04:19.350
I regularly bring back watermelons 
from the fifth level of Telulu.

04:22.490 --> 04:24.860
Hmph. Telulu, huh?

04:26.830 --> 04:28.210
This way.

04:29.900 --> 04:32.500
What's his problem? 
Talk about a bad attitude.

04:35.360 --> 04:39.090
This melon was dropped at 
level 6 or lower in Telulu.

04:39.090 --> 04:41.740
I'm going to turn it into a stray.

04:41.740 --> 04:43.560
If you can defeat it, you pass.

04:43.560 --> 04:48.360
Be ready. This won't be like what 
you've seen on level 5 and up.

04:49.130 --> 04:51.010
Just what I was hoping for.

04:53.910 --> 04:54.490
Here it comes!

04:58.940 --> 05:00.890
That's a steel slime!

05:00.890 --> 05:03.310
It's so hard that blades 
are useless against it!

05:04.870 --> 05:07.420
Still, instead of just 
seeing how things go...

05:07.420 --> 05:09.980
I'll say hello with my rank S strength!

05:14.580 --> 05:16.330
It really is as hard as steel.

05:16.570 --> 05:17.940
Yoda...

05:17.940 --> 05:21.840
No problem. I've got a plan 
that should prove interesting.

05:25.190 --> 05:27.990
All right! Bring it on, steel slime!

05:31.720 --> 05:33.080
A fire bullet!

05:33.080 --> 05:35.390
But it doesn't seem to be working!

05:35.390 --> 05:37.560
No, it just hasn't started to yet!

05:38.780 --> 05:40.820
A freezing bullet this time?

05:42.420 --> 05:44.690
Emily, watch this.

05:44.690 --> 05:45.540
See?

05:48.820 --> 05:51.230
What?! How'd you do that?!

05:51.230 --> 05:53.040
An extreme temperature difference.

05:53.040 --> 05:55.130
Hitting it with a powerful fire bullet,

05:55.130 --> 05:57.570
then immediately freezing 
it with a freezing bullet,

05:57.570 --> 06:00.170
weakens metal by making it brittle.

06:00.170 --> 06:01.840
Wow...

06:01.840 --> 06:03.460
Incredible...

06:03.460 --> 06:05.990
You're really something, bro!

06:06.390 --> 06:09.090
You have my approval as an examiner!

06:09.090 --> 06:11.310
Your Secro license for levels 6 
and below is approved!

06:11.310 --> 06:12.710
Congratulations!

06:13.490 --> 06:15.720
So this is my license.

06:15.720 --> 06:17.980
Congratulations, Yoda!

06:17.980 --> 06:20.400
I've been working here for over ten years,

06:20.400 --> 06:22.300
and I've never been so impressed!

06:22.300 --> 06:24.530
Secro's future is bright!

06:24.530 --> 06:26.790
To make this the most effective...

06:26.790 --> 06:28.510
To get those as drops...

06:28.510 --> 06:29.740
Yoda?

06:29.740 --> 06:32.900
Oh, right. I have some preparations to make.

06:32.900 --> 06:33.930
Emily!

06:34.390 --> 06:35.700
I need your help!

06:35.700 --> 06:37.900
There's something I want!

06:38.160 --> 06:41.000
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

06:39.230 --> 06:41.550
We finally made it here.

06:41.550 --> 06:42.880
All right!

06:45.650 --> 06:49.910
When you said you needed 1.5 million 
pilos because you wanted a tuna,

06:49.910 --> 06:51.590
you really threw me for a loop.

06:51.860 --> 06:54.490
There's something I really want to try.

06:54.490 --> 06:57.770
And the first step to doing that 
is turning this into a stray.

06:59.090 --> 07:00.420
Yes! There it goes!

07:01.400 --> 07:03.360
The stray that comes from a tuna is...

07:05.530 --> 07:08.770
the same kind of gorilla 
that attacked Secro!

07:09.390 --> 07:11.850
Don't worry! Let me handle this!

07:11.850 --> 07:13.790
First, a freezing bullet...

07:14.820 --> 07:17.090
to immobilize it!

07:20.120 --> 07:23.040
Sorry, pal! I gotta use 
the gun I got from you...

07:23.040 --> 07:24.890
to kill you!

07:29.940 --> 07:32.440
Th-That was amazing, Yoda!

07:32.440 --> 07:35.930
That first gorilla gave you so much trouble, 
but you beat this one in no time!

07:38.560 --> 07:41.270
Yes! Just like I thought!

07:41.270 --> 07:44.420
Gorillas drop guns and regular bullets.

07:44.420 --> 07:46.510
Now I can dual wield!

07:46.510 --> 07:50.080
This'll make special bullet 
combos a lot easier!

07:50.660 --> 07:52.270
Two guns at once...

07:52.540 --> 07:57.080
Y-Yoda, please don't end up turning evil!

07:58.200 --> 07:58.910
Huh?

07:58.910 --> 08:01.500
H-Hey, come on! It'll be fine!

08:01.500 --> 08:04.720
I'll always be peaceful 
as long as you're around!

08:10.540 --> 08:12.190
Did something happen?

08:12.830 --> 08:15.890
Actually... a strike has been called.

08:15.890 --> 08:18.710
<i>Doesn't sound like things 
have been peaceful here.</i>

08:18.710 --> 08:21.270
The Adalberd Group occupies 
level 6 of Silicon,

08:21.270 --> 08:23.610
the only place you can get rice,

08:23.610 --> 08:27.060
and they're saying that if I don't 
raise the price of Secro rice,

08:27.060 --> 08:29.010
they won't sell me any more.

08:29.010 --> 08:30.540
I see.

08:34.970 --> 08:38.850
<i>I guess I should find whoever's 
in charge and talk to them.</i>

08:38.850 --> 08:41.030
Hey, if it isn't Sato.

08:41.030 --> 08:42.820
You're...

08:43.300 --> 08:44.470
Neptune!

08:44.470 --> 08:46.110
What're you doing here?

08:46.110 --> 08:49.590
You must be here because 
of Adalberd, too, right?

08:49.590 --> 08:51.470
Yeah. You, too?

08:51.470 --> 08:52.880
By request.

08:52.880 --> 08:54.060
Request?

08:54.390 --> 08:59.480
Adalberd's done this lots of times.

08:59.900 --> 09:03.800
The people in town have 
finally run out of patience.

09:03.800 --> 09:07.200
So the Neptune Group might 
just get rid of them?

09:07.200 --> 09:08.800
No, not quite.

09:09.480 --> 09:11.650
We won't get rid of them. 
We'll destroy them.

09:12.820 --> 09:14.460
I have a question.

09:14.460 --> 09:15.390
What is it?

09:15.390 --> 09:17.070
Would you let me handle this?

09:17.070 --> 09:19.240
Let you... destroy them?

09:19.540 --> 09:20.690
Get rid of them.

09:22.620 --> 09:26.370
<b>Silicon Level 6</b>

09:24.450 --> 09:26.370
This is what's wrong with you!

09:26.370 --> 09:28.250
You gotta really go in there and...

09:28.710 --> 09:30.300
Halt! Who goes there?!

09:30.600 --> 09:32.470
Entry to this level is forbidden!

09:34.630 --> 09:36.330
You're gonna use force?!

09:36.330 --> 09:40.070
Get out here, boys! The townies
 are trying to muscle their way in!

10:00.270 --> 10:02.020
Well, that worked out.

10:02.020 --> 10:03.460
Hey, what's that?

10:03.920 --> 10:06.110
Don't just pop up behind me!

10:06.680 --> 10:10.300
This is a healing bullet. 
All it does is heal wounds,

10:10.550 --> 10:13.500
but when you fuse two together, 
it becomes a sleep bullet,

10:13.500 --> 10:15.410
and it puts your target to sleep.

10:15.410 --> 10:21.430
<i>Yep! This is the new potential that 
came about when I got a second gun!</i>

10:21.260 --> 10:24.010
<b>Arsenic Level 1</b>

10:24.000 --> 10:26.770
What can you do with two guns?

10:27.470 --> 10:30.120
I tested out all kinds of 
different possibilities.

10:33.870 --> 10:36.620
That was amazing! What did you do?

10:36.620 --> 10:39.720
I shot a freezing bullet and a 
fire bullet at the same time.

10:39.720 --> 10:42.740
Looks like that turns them 
into an erasing bullet.

10:42.740 --> 10:44.830
Erasing bullet! That's so cool!

10:45.070 --> 10:48.590
And the combination is just a 
freezing bullet and a fire bullet?

10:50.530 --> 10:53.130
What Emily said gave me a hint,

10:53.130 --> 10:56.560
so I tried several different 
bullet combinations.

10:56.560 --> 11:00.460
The possibilities for bullet 
fusions are basically endless.

11:01.610 --> 11:05.050
Getting a second gun gave that to me.

11:05.400 --> 11:08.720
Wow, so you're doubling their healing power.

11:08.720 --> 11:10.350
Exactly.

11:11.250 --> 11:13.590
Well, guess we should 
carry these guys outside.

11:13.590 --> 11:15.930
Since you followed me down here, 
you'd better help out.

11:15.930 --> 11:17.180
Aw...

11:20.830 --> 11:24.460
So that's the infamous Ryota Sato, is it?

11:25.760 --> 11:27.580
We're just waiting together...

11:27.700 --> 11:29.830
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:27.700 --> 11:29.830
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:28.530 --> 11:29.620
Tee-hee.

11:31.090 --> 11:33.850
I don't want to do any more eyecatches!

11:32.710 --> 11:35.040
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:32.710 --> 11:35.040
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:35.050 --> 11:36.850
Thank you for coming by.

11:36.850 --> 11:40.540
I'm Clint Gray, the dungeon chief of Secro.

11:40.810 --> 11:42.250
Dungeon chief?

11:42.250 --> 11:44.000
Doesn't ring a bell?

11:44.000 --> 11:47.720
It means I hold a pretty high 
position here in Secro.

11:47.720 --> 11:48.780
Uh-huh...

11:48.780 --> 11:50.570
Now, let's cut to the chase.

11:50.570 --> 11:52.840
I'd like to ask a favor of you.

11:52.840 --> 11:53.640
A favor?

11:53.640 --> 11:58.120
Yes. I'd like to enlist your aid 
in a battle for a new dungeon

11:58.120 --> 12:00.540
against the neighboring city of Hetero.

12:00.540 --> 12:02.730
A battle for a new dungeon?

12:02.730 --> 12:07.940
All the dungeons east of 
Secro have meat as drops.

12:07.940 --> 12:10.420
And as you know, 
Hetero is the livestock city.

12:10.420 --> 12:11.720
<i>I don't, actually...</i>

12:11.720 --> 12:17.010
A new dungeon was found halfway 
between Hetero and Secro.

12:17.280 --> 12:22.740
Remarkably, the drops in this dungeon 
are half vegetables and half meat.

12:22.740 --> 12:26.600
If vegetables made up more than half, 
Secro could claim it, but...

12:26.920 --> 12:30.880
<i>Huh... They decide ownership of 
dungeons by the ratio of the drops?</i>

12:31.390 --> 12:32.660
<i>But...</i>

12:32.660 --> 12:36.940
Is it absolutely necessary to 
pick which city it'll belong to?

12:37.790 --> 12:41.600
Every time dropped items are 
purchased, a tax is charged!

12:41.600 --> 12:45.650
Ownership of dungeons makes a huge 
difference in a town's economic health!

12:47.050 --> 12:48.570
S-Sorry...

12:50.560 --> 12:53.110
No, I apologize for losing my composure.

12:53.110 --> 12:54.930
Let me cool down for a moment.

13:00.700 --> 13:02.570
Mm, sweet!

13:02.570 --> 13:04.390
Sugar is the best!

13:05.070 --> 13:08.550
<i>Is he not afraid of diabetes at all?</i>

13:08.820 --> 13:12.460
Anyway, since vegetables and meat 
are dropped in equal proportions,

13:12.460 --> 13:16.850
we decided to determine its ownership 
based on who gets more rare drops.

13:16.850 --> 13:20.940
Which is why, since you're renowned for 
your strength and high drop rates,

13:20.940 --> 13:23.060
I chose you to help.

13:23.910 --> 13:25.990
I won't ask you to do 
it for free, of course.

13:25.990 --> 13:28.030
Even if we lose, 
you'll get a monetary reward,

13:28.030 --> 13:32.420
and if we win, all dropped items you receive 
henceforth will be exempt from taxation.

13:32.420 --> 13:35.710
What do you say? Will you accept?

13:36.020 --> 13:41.120
<i>It makes me feel good to have my work 
recognized and be depended on like this.</i>

13:41.390 --> 13:43.310
<i>I'll need my guns,</i>

13:43.310 --> 13:46.420
<i>and I should have plenty 
of special bullets ready.</i>

13:46.420 --> 13:49.520
<i>That just leaves the magic cart,
 a change of clothes...</i>

13:51.650 --> 13:54.300
Kinda feels like I'm getting 
ready for a business trip.

13:55.050 --> 13:57.070
<i>Back then, I worked too hard</i>

13:57.070 --> 13:58.990
<i>and pushed my own limits too far...</i>

13:59.730 --> 14:02.240
<i>But now, I have Emily with me.</i>

14:02.760 --> 14:03.810
Emily?

14:05.130 --> 14:06.260
Right!

14:07.930 --> 14:09.190
That's the story.

14:09.510 --> 14:12.400
So I'll be going to this new dungeon, Selen.

14:12.400 --> 14:14.130
That's amazing, Yoda!

14:14.130 --> 14:16.100
Just like the Neptune Group!

14:16.100 --> 14:19.630
Being asked to inspect a 
dungeon is a big deal!

14:19.630 --> 14:23.030
Oh, yeah. It was the same way 
with Nihonium, wasn't it?

14:23.030 --> 14:24.380
Understood!

14:24.740 --> 14:28.140
I'll hold down the fort while you're away!

14:28.400 --> 14:30.560
No, I want you to come with me.

14:30.560 --> 14:32.650
What? You do?

14:32.650 --> 14:33.480
Yeah.

14:33.480 --> 14:36.280
But I won't be of any use there.

14:36.280 --> 14:37.470
That's not true!

14:38.010 --> 14:40.320
I want you to come with me.

14:45.200 --> 14:47.540
Low-Level! Carrots!

14:47.540 --> 14:48.510
Eve?!

14:48.510 --> 14:50.580
What will you do about carrots?!

14:50.580 --> 14:54.400
Okay, okay! We'll get as many 
as you need before we leave!

14:54.400 --> 14:56.580
Heh! Better believe it!

14:59.370 --> 15:00.630
There's nothing here.

15:00.630 --> 15:05.510
The only things that don't become 
strays are air, water, and earth.

15:05.510 --> 15:08.480
Other than places with lots of people, 
like towns and dungeons,

15:08.480 --> 15:10.270
it's like this everywhere.

15:10.270 --> 15:11.250
I see.

15:11.830 --> 15:14.870
There's seriously nothing 
here at all, though.

15:14.870 --> 15:16.720
This world is so weird...

15:17.670 --> 15:19.650
Emily? What are you doing?

15:19.650 --> 15:22.350
Traveling from town to town is strenuous.

15:22.910 --> 15:25.830
If anyone travels through here after us,

15:25.830 --> 15:28.840
I hope this will bring them a bit of cheer.

15:29.350 --> 15:33.450
<i>Round, round, the sun is big and round...</i>

15:33.780 --> 15:38.610
<i>Two of them together make 
big, soft cushions!</i>

15:39.040 --> 15:42.040
<i>Oh! There's a cane sticking out of the sofa!</i>

15:42.830 --> 15:47.710
A cane is there to hold you up!

15:47.710 --> 15:48.880
Here... and there...

15:49.660 --> 15:53.050
Oh! We have to add pupils to the eyes!

15:53.360 --> 15:54.460
Ahem!

15:55.450 --> 15:59.110
And now it's all done!

16:00.680 --> 16:03.180
Wh-What is this?

16:04.040 --> 16:05.370
It's Mr. Bean Sprout!

16:05.770 --> 16:08.200
Bean sprouts are a source of energy!

16:08.200 --> 16:10.260
I... I see.

16:10.260 --> 16:11.610
Then, I'll draw something, too.

16:13.120 --> 16:15.320
You're very good at drawing!

16:15.320 --> 16:17.030
That's a cute bean sprout!

16:17.030 --> 16:19.840
W-Well, yours is cute, too!

16:25.140 --> 16:27.090
Now it's perfect!

16:27.090 --> 16:29.540
Okay, ready to get moving again?

16:29.540 --> 16:30.690
Yes!

16:33.510 --> 16:36.930
You can do it!

16:37.640 --> 16:40.840
Yoda! Hold up that side, please!

16:40.840 --> 16:42.550
S-Sure.

16:42.550 --> 16:43.900
And... hup!

16:43.900 --> 16:45.850
There! All done!

16:46.160 --> 16:48.200
<i>That backpack had...</i>

16:48.200 --> 16:50.330
<i>a tent this big in it?!</i>

16:50.330 --> 16:53.190
This is where I get to show my real skills!

16:53.190 --> 16:55.620
Could you go and fetch some water, please?

16:55.620 --> 16:56.530
Sure.

17:03.150 --> 17:05.320
<i>What the heck is going on in there?</i>

17:08.450 --> 17:11.660
Now that I'm used to living 
in a house with Emily,

17:11.660 --> 17:14.740
roughing it in the wilderness 
like this is a big change.

17:14.740 --> 17:17.380
I have up early to go find carrots, too.

17:17.380 --> 17:19.300
Nice job, Low-Level.

17:19.570 --> 17:21.620
I hope I got enough of them...

17:21.620 --> 17:23.860
Yoda! It's all done!

17:26.860 --> 17:29.780
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What the heck is all this?!

17:29.780 --> 17:32.180
<i>A warm light illuminating the tent...</i>

17:32.180 --> 17:35.080
<i>A relaxing sofa brimming 
with a sense of security...</i>

17:35.080 --> 17:38.610
<i>And the most amazing cooking is sitting 
here as if it's a matter of course!</i>

17:38.610 --> 17:41.980
<i>Even in a tent, Emily's house 
has an overwhelming presence!</i>

17:43.670 --> 17:45.900
Wait, it doesn't make sense!

17:45.900 --> 17:48.000
How in the world did you carry all this?

17:48.000 --> 17:48.910
Huh?

17:49.610 --> 17:51.800
I packed it in my backpack.

17:51.800 --> 17:53.330
It was pretty heavy.

17:54.420 --> 17:57.180
<i>What kind of backpack 
does she have, exactly?</i>

17:57.180 --> 17:59.720
Oh! There's dessert for after dinner, too!

18:01.240 --> 18:03.880
Since we're on our first trip together,

18:04.270 --> 18:06.450
I was so happy, I gave it extra effort.

18:06.770 --> 18:08.860
So precious!

18:07.980 --> 18:10.190
<b>Ryota abandoned all thought!</b>

18:08.860 --> 18:09.800
Huh?

18:11.520 --> 18:14.800
Oh, right. I'll go burn our trash.

18:14.800 --> 18:17.560
Burn it? Not throw it out?

18:17.560 --> 18:20.140
That's right. I'm incinerating it.

18:20.140 --> 18:23.320
In town, there are people who do it for us,

18:23.320 --> 18:26.280
but at times like these, 
we have to do it ourselves.

18:26.280 --> 18:28.750
We don't want things turning into strays.

18:28.750 --> 18:30.910
Even trash turns into strays?

18:30.910 --> 18:34.330
And the strays that come from 
trash are really strong.

18:34.330 --> 18:36.920
They're different monsters 
than they originally were.

18:36.920 --> 18:39.520
Different monsters come from trash?

18:39.520 --> 18:43.460
Burning trash is a very important job.

18:43.460 --> 18:46.640
If I were to kill one of those strays...

18:46.640 --> 18:48.260
Do you think something might happen?

18:53.030 --> 18:54.980
The stray our trash turned into...

18:55.500 --> 18:58.090
It's... a Frankenstein?!

18:58.090 --> 18:59.160
I'll hold it here!

19:01.780 --> 19:03.240
Emily, stand back!

19:03.240 --> 19:04.170
Right!

19:04.170 --> 19:05.850
We'll start with this one!

19:06.320 --> 19:08.590
Burn it to ashes, fire bullet!

19:08.980 --> 19:11.390
It didn't work! The flames are too weak!

19:11.390 --> 19:14.340
If one isn't enough, how about this?!

19:14.340 --> 19:15.090
That's...

19:25.680 --> 19:28.420
They always make such a loud sound.

19:28.420 --> 19:30.720
These fused bullets really 
are gonna be handy.

19:30.720 --> 19:32.720
Yes! They're amazing!

19:32.720 --> 19:33.570
Now...

19:49.250 --> 19:53.110
Yoda, did that shot just... curve?

19:53.110 --> 19:53.990
Yeah.

19:53.990 --> 19:56.980
More like the bullet chased 
the slime, actually.

19:56.980 --> 19:58.980
It's a homing bullet!

19:59.650 --> 20:03.350
Yoda's gained yet another 
dangerous weapon...

20:05.060 --> 20:10.170
So this is Selen, the new dungeon 
halfway between Secro and Hetero!

20:10.550 --> 20:12.600
It's so busy here.

20:12.600 --> 20:16.350
Yeah, 'cause people have been 
sent in from both towns.

20:19.940 --> 20:22.060
Emily, isn't that...

20:22.060 --> 20:23.620
A pile of trash, it looks like.

20:23.930 --> 20:27.580
With so many people here, 
there's bound to be lots of trash.

20:27.840 --> 20:30.740
Is it okay to just leave it there?

20:31.260 --> 20:34.110
It's probably fine since there 
are so many people here,

20:34.110 --> 20:37.070
but it's still scary, isn't it? 
Like a ticking time bomb.

20:38.200 --> 20:39.370
Burn.

20:41.520 --> 20:43.880
Fire Magic: Inferno!

20:51.050 --> 20:54.880
She must be in charge of gathering up 
all the trash and burning it.

20:55.360 --> 20:57.670
What incredible magic power.

20:59.800 --> 21:00.640
Whoa...

21:00.640 --> 21:02.850
The next trash pile is already that big?

21:02.850 --> 21:04.330
It's so much!

21:04.560 --> 21:08.780
<i>She can't burn enough to keep up 
with this kind of trash production!</i>

21:13.410 --> 21:16.240
No! We have to stop her right now!

21:16.240 --> 21:16.830
Huh?

21:16.830 --> 21:19.790
<i>Those bags under her eyes... 
And she's so pale.</i>

21:19.790 --> 21:23.460
<i>That's what people who've put in over 
100 hours of overtime in a month look like!</i>

21:24.390 --> 21:26.480
<i>Just like... when I...</i>

21:26.760 --> 21:27.720
Let's go!

21:27.720 --> 21:28.830
Okay!

21:33.600 --> 21:35.180
Are you all right?

21:35.970 --> 21:37.810
Adventurers?

21:38.350 --> 21:41.650
If you have trash, 
just bring it all here, okay?

21:41.650 --> 21:45.400
Sure, but... you should rest for a while!

21:45.400 --> 21:48.790
Thank you, but I can't do that.

21:48.790 --> 21:51.310
I have to burn the trash right away.

21:51.310 --> 21:52.620
But...

21:52.620 --> 21:53.820
I'm all right.

21:56.140 --> 21:58.580
Fire Magic: Inferno!

22:06.490 --> 22:07.550
Are you okay?!
